.TH AFPRUSTD 8 "November 2026" "afprust 0.1.3" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
afprustd \- AFP 2.2 (AppleShare over TCP/IP) file server for classic Mac OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B afprustd
.RB [ \-F
.IR config ]
.RB [ \-t ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-V ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B afprustd
serves files to Mac OS 8 and 9 (AppleShare Client 3.7 and later) using the
Apple Filing Protocol version 2.2 over TCP/IP. It reads netatalk 3/4
.I afp.conf
files and netatalk 2
.I afpd.conf
/
.I AppleVolumes.default
files, and stores Finder information, comments and resource forks in the
same places as netatalk, so volumes can be shared with netatalk and
Mac OS X clients.
.PP
The master process accepts connections and starts one process per client.
Each session process authenticates the user through PAM (service
.IR afprust )
and then permanently switches to that user's uid and groups before it
accesses any volume. All volume access is confined to the volume by the
kernel (openat2 RESOLVE_BENEATH).
.PP
With
.B appletalk = yes
a small helper process gives the Ethernet interface an AppleTalk address and
answers Chooser lookups, so the server appears in the Mac OS Chooser. Macs
then connect over TCP/IP.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-F " config"
Use this configuration file. Without it, afprustd uses the first that
exists of
.IR /etc/afprust/afp.conf ,
.IR /etc/netatalk/afp.conf ,
and the netatalk 2 files
.IR /etc/netatalk/afpd.conf " and " /etc/netatalk/AppleVolumes.default .
A path ending in
.I afpd.conf
selects the netatalk 2 format.
.TP
.B \-t
Check the configuration, print a summary including ignored options, and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Log debug messages.
.TP
.B \-d
Accepted for netatalk compatibility; afprustd always runs in the foreground.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration. New sessions use the new settings.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Notify connected clients that the server is shutting down and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/afprust/afp.conf
Main configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/afprust/extmap.conf
File extension to type/creator mapping.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/afprust
PAM configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/default/afprustd
Extra command line options for the systemd service.
.TP
.I /var/lib/afprust/afp_signature
Server signature (identifies this server to clients).
.SH SECURITY
DHCAST128 is the strongest authentication classic Mac OS supports; its
128-bit Diffie-Hellman group is weak by modern standards. Cleartext
authentication sends passwords unencrypted. Use the server on trusted
networks only. Logins as root are refused. Repeated failed logins from one
address block it for 15 minutes.
.PP
The configuration options are documented in
.I /usr/share/doc/afprust/CONFIGURATION.md
and at https://github.com/adamf/afprust/blob/main/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR afp.conf (5)
from netatalk,
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR pam (8)
